---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  serviceType: 'Custom automation builds for small business',
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Vemor', url: 'https://vemor.ai' },
  description: 'Fixed-scope custom automation for small businesses: one workflow, built on your existing tools, quoted before the build starts. Reconciliation, databases, document pipelines, outreach automation.',
  areaServed: ['United States', 'Mexico'],
};
---
<Base
  title="Custom Automation Builds for Small Business | San Diego | Vemor"
  description="Fixed-scope AI automation for small business: reconciliation, document pipelines, outreach. Built on the tools you already use. San Diego-based, serving the US and Mexico."
  schema={schema}
  path="/builds"
>
  <section class="hero" style="min-height:0; padding-bottom:60px;">
    <span class="hero-tagline">Custom Builds</span>
    <h1>One problem.<br /><span class="gold">Solved for good.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Not every business needs a full operations partner on day one. Sometimes one
      task is eating your week, and it just needs to die. A custom build is a single
      system with a fixed scope and a clear price, built on the tools you already use.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="https://Vemor.as.me/" class="btn-primary">Book a Discovery Call</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EXAMPLES -->
  <div class="section-full soft">
    <div class="inner">
      <span class="label">What a Build Looks Like</span>
      <h2 class="title">Real systems, running today.</h2>
      <div class="cards-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>A reconciliation engine</h3>
          <p>Reads the client's existing point-of-sale database every night, reconciles sales across four locations, flags payment errors and unauthorized discounts, and emails a finished report before opening. What used to be a full-time job is now an hour of review.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>A document pipeline</h3>
          <p>Reads hundreds of legal filings for a law practice, extracts the numbers with evidence behind every figure, validates them with hard arithmetic rules, and produces a benchmark report in seconds. Work that used to take hours per case.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>An asset tracker</h3>
          <p>RFID tracking for rental equipment across four physical locations. Readers at each site, cloud sync, cross-checking against invoices, and a text alert at closing when a unit is missing. Hardware and software, delivered as one working system.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
  <section>
    <span class="label">How It Works</span>
    <h2 class="title">Scope first. Price before build. No surprises.</h2>
    <div class="steps steps-4">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <h3>Audit</h3>
        <p>A paid operations audit: a few days inside your workflow, then a written plan of what to automate, what it costs, and what it saves. The plan is yours either way.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <h3>Fixed quote</h3>
        <p>You get the scope and the price before anything gets built. If we missed the estimate, that's Vemor's problem, not yours.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <h3>Build &amp; prove</h3>
        <p>Built on your existing tools and tested against your real work, not demo data. It ships when it survives your actual Tuesday.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">4</div>
        <h3>Your choice</h3>
        <p>Take the keys: documentation included, the system is yours. Or have Vemor run it as a managed service and never think about it again.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FIT -->
  <div class="section-full soft">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="story-grid">
        <div class="story-content">
          <h4>Good fit for a build</h4>
          <p>
            You know exactly what hurts: the nightly close-out, the quote follow-ups,
            the spreadsheet nobody trusts, the report that takes all Friday. One
            defined problem, one defined win. Many clients start here and grow into
            <a href="/operations" style="color:var(--gold);">Managed AI Operations</a>
            once the first system proves itself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="story-content">
          <h4>The same promise applies</h4>
          <p>
            Every build sits on top of what you already have. Your data stays yours,
            the documentation comes with it, and nothing requires Vemor to stay
            useful. We earn the next project by delivering this one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section style="text-align:center;">
    <h2 class="title">Got a task that needs to die?</h2>
    <p class="sub" style="margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;">
      Tell us what it is. Twenty minutes, and you'll get a straight answer on whether
      a build is worth it. Sometimes the honest answer is a spreadsheet fix and a
      handshake.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas" style="justify-content:center;">
      <a href="https://Vemor.as.me/" class="btn-primary">Book a Discovery Call</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary">Send a Message</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
